# Element Armory Figma Plugin — Phased Tasks

## Phase 1 — Plugin Foundation (1–2 days)
- [ ] Initialize plugin with Vite + React + TypeScript
- [ ] Add manifest.json (name, id, main, ui)
- [ ] Implement main.ts: showUI, onmessage stub
- [ ] Create src/ui/App.tsx shell
- [ ] Wire UI to dist/ui.html and main to dist/main.js
- [ ] Verify plugin loads in Figma

## Phase 2 — API Integration (Mocked First)
- [ ] Define ElementItem type (id, name, html, css, preview, createdAt)
- [ ] Add api.ts with fetchElements() mock
- [ ] Add placeholder for GET /api/elements and GET /api/elements/:id
- [ ] Optional: add Zod schemas for validation

## Phase 3 — Fast UI List (Performance Critical)
- [ ] Add search input (filter by name/source)
- [ ] Build ElementCard: thumbnail, title, meta, Insert + Preview
- [ ] Build ElementList using react-virtual (virtualized list)
- [ ] Add useElements hook (data + filter state)
- [ ] Lazy load preview images when visible
- [ ] Match extension library layout: card grid, spacing, tokens

## Phase 4 — Insert Element into Figma
- [ ] Define postMessage types (INSERT_ELEMENT, etc.)
- [ ] UI: send INSERT_ELEMENT on Insert click
- [ ] Main: handle INSERT_ELEMENT → createFrame, resize, name, append, scrollIntoView
- [ ] Initially: HTML → frame placeholder only

## Phase 5 — HTML → Figma Rendering (Core Feature)
- [ ] Decide strategy: Option A (SVG snapshot) vs Option B (DOM → nodes)
- [ ] MVP: implement SVG snapshot path (HTML → render → SVG → Figma image)
- [ ] Optional later: DOM → Figma node mapping (div→frame, img→rectangle, text→text)

## Phase 6 — Component System
- [ ] Create Figma component instead of raw frame on insert
- [ ] Insert instance on canvas
- [ ] Name and structure for designer reuse

## Phase 7 — Auth + Sync
- [ ] Add login UI (placeholder or OAuth flow)
- [ ] Store token via figma.clientStorage.setAsync("token", token)
- [ ] Replace mock API with real GET /api/elements + Authorization header
- [ ] Handle token refresh / logout

## Phase 8 — Developer-Focused Features
- [ ] Code panel: show HTML, CSS, React, Tailwind (optional)
- [ ] Copy to clipboard for code snippets
- [ ] “Open in Element Armory” deep link to web app

## Phase 9 — Future: Figma → HTML
- [ ] Select component → export node tree → convert to HTML → send to API
- [ ] Extract layout, styles, text, images

## Phase 10 — Performance Optimizations
- [ ] Lazy previews (load images when in viewport)
- [ ] TanStack Query for caching elements
- [ ] Batch node creation where possible
- [ ] Keep heavy logic in UI thread, not main

## Phase 11 — Plugin Listing
- [ ] Finalize name: "Element Armory – UI to Code Components"
- [ ] Keywords: html, css, ui components, developer, frontend
- [ ] Target audience: frontend devs, AI coding users
